messages.body_plain:
Dear all,

I just wanted to make sure about one thing whether my Stan code is correct or not.

It is just a basic question. Your help is greatly appreciated.

x has a bivariate standard normal distribution.

The limit state function (g(x)) works as a variable into the likelihood :

likelihood function = (1/sqrt(2*pi)) * exp [(-1/2) g^2] , where g = 3 - (sum(x)/sqrt(2)) and the Gaussian prior is on x ( x ~ normal (0,1)).

my Stan code:
data{
}
parameters {
  vector[2] x;
}

transformed parameters {
real g = 3 - (sum(x)/sqrt(2));
}

model {
//Gaussian prior
  x ~ normal(0, 1);
//likelihood
  g ~ normal(0, 1);
}

Is the above Stan code correct?

Thank you for your consideration.

Hamed
